According to Home Assistant coding guidelines, error messages should not end with periods. The exception messages in this file are inconsistent - some end with periods while others don't. For consistency and adherence to guidelines, all exception messages should not end with periods.

Messages that should have their trailing periods removed:
- "No users found, please check Protect permissions." → "No users found, please check Protect permissions"
- "Only music media type is supported." → "Only music media type is supported"
- "Could not find privacy zone with name {zone_name} on camera {camera_name}." → "Could not find privacy zone with name {zone_name} on camera {camera_name}"
- "Your UniFi Protect version ({current_version}) is too old. Minimum required: {min_version}." → Should keep the period after "old" as it separates two sentences, but remove the final period
```suggestion
      "message": "No users found, please check Protect permissions"
    },
    "only_music_supported": {
      "message": "Only music media type is supported"
